# tools/al/ales_dc_remove_witness.rish — the DC-offset remover: subtract the span's mean from every sample, y = saturate(x − mean), a pure translation
# (ALES90).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES90.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-222356_fill-ales90-lotus-dc-offset-remover.md
# Stands on: lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_min/max, the one true saturate) and lotus/rectify.rye (ALES84 — the full-wave rectifier whose
# introduced DC offset this rung undoes, the composition proof). The DRIVE family's even-harmonic generators (the rectifiers ALES84/85/86, the asymmetric
# tube drive ALES82, the 1-bit crush ALES81) each shift the signal's mean off zero; nothing yet took that offset back out — this rung does.
#
# lotus/dc_remove.rye subtracts the span's mean from each sample, saturating at the rails. The crux is that a PURE TRANSLATION preserves every
# sample-to-sample difference exactly — the same constant leaves every sample, so only the mean moves and the waveform shape (all its AC content) carries
# through untouched (distinct from ALES2's gain, which scales the differences). The mean is truncated toward zero, so the residual mean magnitude is
# strictly less than one LSB (|Σ y| < count): a zero-mean signal is unchanged exactly, and the remove is idempotent where nothing saturates. The selftest
# proves it: it removes a pure DC offset (a constant span → 0); a zero-mean signal is unchanged exactly; the translation preserves every adjacent
# difference; the residual mean is bounded below one LSB; it is idempotent where nothing saturates; it undoes the rectifier's offset (rectify a symmetric
# wave → a large positive DC → dc_remove restores a near-zero mean); saturation at the rail is honest (a max sample under a negative mean pins, never
# wraps); the span discipline holds; the empty span is a clean no-op (no divide by zero); a span past the end refuses BadRange, the clip untouched. Purely
# local — sum then subtract in i64, one saturate per sample; no gain, no coefficient, no delay line, no envelope, no frequency, no network, no keys, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_dc_remove_witness.rish

say "ales-dc-remove: Language EN — the DRIVE family's even-harmonic generators (the rectifiers, the asymmetric tube drive, the 1-bit crush) each SHIFT the signal's mean off zero — rectify a symmetric wave and every sample turns positive, the audio riding on a large positive DC offset. A DC offset eats headroom and thumps at a cut seam; every real chain that carries a nonlinearity carries a DC remover right after it. This rung takes that offset back out: subtract the span's MEAN from every sample, y = saturate(x − mean)."
say "ales-dc-remove: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: DC removal is a PURE TRANSLATION, the same constant off every sample, so it PRESERVES EVERY SAMPLE-TO-SAMPLE DIFFERENCE exactly — only the mean moves, the waveform shape (all its AC content) carried through untouched. That is what sets it apart from ALES2's gain, which SCALES the differences. The mean is truncated toward zero, so the residual mean magnitude is strictly less than one LSB (|Σ y| < count): a zero-mean signal is UNCHANGED EXACTLY, and the remove is IDEMPOTENT where nothing saturates. Saturation at the rail is named honestly, never hidden."
say "ales-dc-remove: Lens TAME — one mono clip of i16 PCM DC-removed in place over a span; a two-pass block statistic (sum in i64, then subtract the truncated mean), memoryless (no carried state, no feedback, no delay line), one saturate per sample (ALES2 reused, never a wrap); an empty span is a clean no-op (no divide by zero); a span outside the samples refuses BadRange before any read or write, the clip untouched on refusal; siloed to lotus/, no gain, no coefficient, no envelope, no frequency, no snapshot, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker, no sample rate."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/dc_remove"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/dc_remove.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-dc-remove: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/dc_remove.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-dc-remove: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-dc-remove: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-dc-remove' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-dc-remove: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-dc-remove line"
